pane-recovery-complete-description = The new conversation received a complete response using the available local history. The original conversation is retained. This does not restore the old CLI session or undo tool actions from the interrupted request.
pane-recovery-node-title = Node.js needs attention
pane-recovery-node-description = Open Check setup to install a compatible Node.js version or select its path, then retry. Paths recorded as automatically detected are checked again if an upgrade removes them; manual overrides are preserved.
pane-recovery-cli-title = Provider CLI needs attention
pane-recovery-cli-description = Open Check setup to install the provider CLI or correct its path, then retry. Automatically detected paths can be rediscovered after upgrades; manual overrides are not replaced.
pane-recovery-auth-description = Authentication was rejected. Complete provider login or update credentials in the provider's Advanced settings, then retry. Local program detection does not verify login.
pane-recovery-limit-description = Wait for the provider limit to reset or check your account quota, then retry manually. This request will not be repeated automatically.
pane-recovery-session-title = Previous session is unavailable
pane-recovery-session-description = The native session cannot be resumed. Retry from the available local history in a new conversation; the original is retained. Tool actions may already have run, so review them before retrying.
pane-recovery-connection-title = Connection interrupted
pane-recovery-connection-description = Check your network and proxy, then retry from saved history. Partial output is retained but may be incomplete. A retry starts a new conversation and may repeat tool actions; nothing is resent automatically.
pane-recovery-unknown-title = Request did not complete
pane-recovery-unknown-description = Review the error below. After fixing the cause, retry from saved history in a new conversation. The original is retained, but completed tool actions are not undone and may run again.
pane-cancelled-description = The request was cancelled by the user.
pane-deepseek-install-description = The “dsh web” command only opens DeepSeek’s browser UI. Claudero needs the headless CLI. Use the button below to install it into Claudero’s runtime directory, or install @deepseek-ai/dsh and set the CLI path in Preferences.
